## Noncommercial Use

A commercial use is one that makes or attempts to make a profit or gain any financial advantage. For example, using the software in software-as-a-service or other network services for which you charge a fee is a commercial use. Using the software in your own business to run your business is a commercial use. Distributing the software as part of a product for which you charge a fee is a commercial use.

